    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caupo</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cōpo</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cūpo</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 47</span></i> P.;
		cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 20, 6, 7</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">the form copo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Clu. 59, 163</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4169</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Momms. 5078</span></i>),
				ōnis, m.
			root cap-, to take in, receive, v. capio; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπηλος</span>, <i>a
				petty tradesman</i>, <i>huckster</i>, <i>innkeeper</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul.
				3, 5, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 27, 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				1, 29</span></i> K. and H.; 1, 5, 4; <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
			57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 4, 9, 1 al.</span></i>—*
			</div>
